chnical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAWAI SHOUHEI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KUDOU MITUGU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAMIKI SEIMITU HOUSEKI KABUSIK</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWAI, SHOUHEI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KUDOU, MITUGU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAMIKI SEIMITU HOUSEKI KABUSIKI KAISHA</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAWAI SHOUHEI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KUDOU MITUGU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWAI, SHOUHEI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KUDOU, MITUGU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A coreless motor having an improved assembling accuracy and a high accuracy constituted by reducing the number of metallic parts, the weight, the number of parts, the assembling man-hour, and the manufacturing cost. The device is equipped with a cylindrical outer housing whose one side is closed and which has a through hole (16) at its center. A bearing (3a) on one side for supporting a rotary shaft (2) by a resin molded body (3) fixed and formed via a through hole (1c) of the housing and a bearing housing (3b) fitted and disposed coaxially with the rotary shaft (2) are continuously and integrally formed. A rotor and a stator are assembled by using the resin molded body (3) as a base.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un moteur sans noyau dont l'assemblage et le fonctionnement sont plus précis grâce à la réduction du nombre de pièces métalliques, du poids, du nombre de pièces, du rapport heure-personne pour l'assemblage et du coût de fabrication. Le dispositif est équipé d'un carter externe cylindrique dont un côté est fermé et présentant un orifice passant (16) au niveau de son centre. Un palier (3a), placé sur un côté, est destiné à supporter un arbre rotatif (2) logé dans un corps résineux moulé (3), un orifice passant (1c) est ménagé le long du carter et un boîtier de roulement (3b) est ajusté et disposé de manière coaxiale avec l'arbre rotatif (2), le palier et le boîtier de roulement étant solidaires. Un rotor et un stator sont assemblés à l'aide du corps (3) qui sert de base.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>